.TH "NAVIGATIONTRANSITION.COMMITTED" "3JS" "May 5, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
NavigationTransition.committed \- NavigationTransition: committed
property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]committed\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]NavigationTransition\f[R] interface returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R]
that fulfills when \f[CR]Navigation.currentEntry\f[R] is updated and the
new URL is displayed in the browser, marking the navigation as
committed.
This happens after all precommit handlers for the navigation are
fulfilled.
.PP
The \f[CR]committed\f[R] promise rejects if any precommit handler
rejects.
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves to \f[CR]undefined\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]function\f[R] lockInNavigation() {
  \f[B]await\f[R] navigation.transition.committed;
  \f[I]// Navigation has committed successfully\f[R]
}
.EE
